{"step_index":178,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T07:00:30Z","input_tokens":2786,"cache_read_tokens":90155,"output_tokens":1241,"thinking":"**Interpreting the Command**\n\nI'm currently dissecting the `/plan` command, focusing on its input. It appears to be a garbled request, possibly in Spanish, with a significant amount of typos and extra characters. My initial task is to clean this up and discern the intended meaning, which seems to involve a .bat file and \"rules\" or \"deco\".\n\n\n**Analyzing the Intent**\n\nI've made progress in deciphering the user's intended meaning. It looks like they've opted for the original `.bat` launcher, understanding the limitations of the `.exe`. Furthermore, they seem to be requesting feedback on the automation aspect, specifically, on \"automation,\" from previous communication or context, potentially related to the plan. I'm moving forward with this assumption.\n\n\n**Deciphering the Code**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specifics of \"sssasddd\" and \"ommmftppp,atocp.\" I believe \"sssasddd\" might relate to \"estado\" or perhaps \"dashboard\", while \"ommmftppp,atocp\" seems to be a garbled version of \"comportamiento automático\" or \"omnipresente.\" This is leading me to the phrase \"dame feedback de tu formato automático\".\n\n\n**Confirming the Execution**\n\nI've determined I need to generate and then wait for approval per `/plan`, but the user explicitly said \"actúa\". I've decided to proceed with the `play.bat` creation, which I'll create in the root, and update the plan/artifact with this confirmation. I am confident in the `.bat` file solution and the efficiency of the implementation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"Set-Content play.bat \"@echo off`nTITLE Pizzant - The Humanoid Hunter`nCOLOR 0B`n`necho ==============================================`necho  INICIANDO REGLAS DE PLAY (PIZZANT)`necho =======================================